<title>BELGIUM: UCB opens chemicals plant in Malaysia.</title>
<headline>UCB opens chemicals plant in Malaysia.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-05-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Belgian chemicals and drugs firm UCB said it opened a new 600 million francs factory for speciality chemicals in Seremban, Malaysia, on Thursday.</p>
<p>It said initial annual capacity was 14,000 tonnes of crylcoat polyester resins in powder form, representing a potential turnover of about 1.5 billion francs.</p>
<p>Crylcoat resins are used in paints for the protection of metallic surfaces.</p>
<p>UCB said its annual turnover in Asia exceeded 4.5 billion francs in 1996.</p>
